---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "10 June 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use | Swimly"
  description="The terms that apply when you use swimly.uk, join the waitlist, or apply to the founding clubs programme."
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section class="relative pt-32 pb-16 sm:pt-40 overflow-hidden">
      <div class="dot-grid absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-[480px] pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-tight text-[#0F2D2D] mt-5">Terms of use</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-ink-mute">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
          These terms cover your use of swimly.uk. They are short because this is an informational
          website, not a contract for the Swimly platform itself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pb-20 sm:pb-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12">

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">About this site</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            swimly.uk is the marketing and information site for Swimly, club management software
            for UK swimming clubs, operated from the United Kingdom. You can contact us at
            <a href="mailto:hello@swimly.uk" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline underline-offset-2">hello@swimly.uk</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">Using our content</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            The content on this site, including guides, articles, and downloadable resources, is
            ours unless stated otherwise. You are welcome to share and quote it for your club's
            non-commercial use with a link back to the source. Please do not republish whole
            articles or pass our content off as your own.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">The waitlist and founding clubs programme</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            Joining the waitlist or applying to the founding clubs programme creates no obligation
            on either side. Offers described on this site, such as the founding clubs free period,
            are subject to availability and to a conversation where we both agree Swimly is a good
            fit for your club. Details of how we handle your data are in our
            <a href="/privacy/" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline underline-offset-2">privacy policy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">The club directory</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            Our <a href="/clubs/" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline underline-offset-2">club directory</a>
            is compiled from publicly available information to help families find swimming clubs.
            We do our best to keep it accurate, but clubs change training times, venues, and
            contact details without telling us. Always confirm details with the club directly.
            If you represent a listed club and want your entry corrected or removed, email us.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">Accuracy and liability</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            We work hard to keep the information on this site accurate, including comparisons with
            other products, which we review periodically and date where possible. Competitor
            pricing and features change, so check with the vendor before making decisions.
            Articles on this site are general guidance for club volunteers, not legal, financial,
            or safeguarding advice. To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for losses
            arising from reliance on the content of this site.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">Links to other sites</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            Where we link to other websites, including club websites and governing body resources,
            we are not responsible for their content or their privacy practices.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">Changes and governing law</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            We may update these terms from time to time, and will update the date at the top when
            we do. These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
